        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Have you ever wanted a book but could not find it? Hephzibah, a 12-year-old from Britain, had the same problem. To solve this, she started to write her own books when she was 10."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Hephzibah felt there weren’t enough books with "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "main characters",
            "ref": "v-main-character"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " from "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "minority groups",
            "ref": "v-minority-group"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Her mum gave her an idea. She said, “Don’t just "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "complain",
            "ref": "v-complain"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Try to change it.” Luckily, Hephzibah loved to write. She also had many good ideas. So she started her first book."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Her first book tells the story of a black girl who travels to the future. She must stop robots from taking over the world. Her second book "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "continues",
            "ref": "v-continue"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the adventure. Hephzibah hopes her stories could become a TV show or a film one day."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Now, children can borrow her books from the library. She is also a finalist "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "finalist",
            "zh": "入围决赛者"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the BBC’s "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Make a Difference Awards",
            "zh": "改变世界奖"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " 2025. She is happy that there are more books with minority characters now. “But we still need more,” she says."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
